DISTRIBUTION SHAPE

Veritas is self-contained. It declares no runtime dependencies: the evidence
primitives -- predicate semantics, relation-set writeback validation, the outcome
taxonomy, and the component registry -- are files under veritas_demo/evidence/.

    git clone https://github.com/Wyrd-Flux/veritas
    python -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install .

Nothing else is needed. No environment variables, no source-tree bindings, no
private corpus, no concept graph, no other Wyrd Flux package.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

HISTORY: THIS CODE WAS ONCE A SEPARATE PACKAGE

The evidence primitives were extracted from internal source trees for the public
release, published first as a separate Apache-2.0 package
(Wyrd-Flux/wyrd-evidence-core), and then folded into this repository when it
became clear that package had exactly one consumer.

That repository was archived, not deleted. Its commit history, its own
PROVENANCE.md, and the provenance records it carried remain readable. This
repository's git history was not rewritten either: the adapter-only release and
the separate-core release are both still present.

For code moved into veritas_demo/evidence/, docs/PROVENANCE.md records:

  * the original internal source path for each file
  * the source SHA-256, where one was recorded
  * the public core commit the code passed through
  * the extraction and folding changes, file by file
  * the operator attestation
  * NO_VCS_HISTORY_AT_SOURCE, for the three modules that had none

